id42-agent builds and runs nanobot. nanobot is not relicensed.

Upstream: https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot
Pinned release: v0.4.2
Pinned commit: 0dc8679edcc6061fbcdf3de13c7e16000e9d1b65

The image is produced from that commit's Dockerfile, then id42-work[mcp,postgres,web],
id42-work-odoo, and id42-work-github are installed into a separate virtualenv.
Those connector packages and id42-work are Apache-2.0 and are not relicensed.
The Dockerfile copies nanobot's LICENSE
and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md into the image. Those files stay in every image
this repository builds.

